 ## Overview
-Sparse Coding with K-SVD compresses volume rendering data by learning an overcomplete dictionary from rendered images and representing image blocks as sparse linear combinations of dictionary atoms [S2, unofficial]. It differs from prescribed basis methods (like DCT) by adapting the basis to the specific statistical properties of the volume rendering output, yielding higher reconstruction fidelity (PSNR) for the same or lower bitrates, particularly in scenarios involving missing data or high compression ratios [S2, unofficial]. It builds on [Compression](4-compression.md) by providing a data-dependent transformation stage.
+Sparse Coding with K-SVD compresses volume rendering data by learning an overcomplete dictionary from rendered images and representing image blocks as sparse linear combinations of dictionary atoms [S2, unofficial]. It differs from prescribed basis methods (like DCT) by adapting the basis to the specific statistical properties of the volume rendering output, yielding higher reconstruction fidelity (PSNR) for the same or lower bitrates, particularly in scenarios involving missing data or high compression ratios [S2, unofficial].
 
